      "content": "Yeah, confirmed. Just to be clear on the scope: IT specifically mentioned they want a clean slate to avoid any data drift from the old study affecting the new one. That means the local weight distributions and the non-indexed correlation matrices used for the longitudinal modeling are included in the wipe. They don't want any legacy \"noise\" hanging around in the active memory or the temp arrays. Sound good?",
